1x3s|n|One who, or that which, springs; specifically, one who rouses game. ; A young plant. ; The impost, or point at which an arch rests upon its support, and from which it seems to spring. ; The bottom stone of an arch, which lies on the impost. The skew back is one form of springer. ; The rib of a groined vault, as being the solid abutment for each section of vaulting. ; The grampus. ; A variety of the field spaniel. See Spaniel. ; A species of antelope; the sprinkbok.	a:1b10,1,3~1b10,1,3	V:1mo9,23,5;fnc,22,2;1mob,20,2;1e3p,18,3~1mo9,23,5;1e3p,18,3;1mob,20,2;fnc,22,2	n:1moa,48,5;7fd,12,4~1moa,48,5;7fd,12,4	N:786,94,3;1tqi,58,3;1bya,45,3;15m5,40,4;8k5,36,5;16ap,35,3;1uzo,30,3;enw,21,3;4qw,16,2;18db,15,3~8k5,36,5;1g7i,3,4;15m5,40,4;1tqi,58,3;1uzo,30,3;enw,21,3;18db,15,3;786,94,3;16ap,35,3;1bya,45,3
